A1. This marks where the yegg dropped. ~ SPOT
A5. How a good many relieve the distressed. ~ ROB
A8. This fish will criticize your line. ~ CARP
A12. Dobbin's third speed forward. ~ LOPE
A13. Rodent found hopping in March. ~ HARE
A14. Sahara taxi. ~ CAMEL
A15. What all the "Ins" will someday be. ~ OUTS
A16. Fire stone. ~ OPAL
A17. Bull grounds. ~ ARENA
A18. Big paper and pen man. ~ WRITER
A20. The first thing that strikes you about a cedar trunk. ~ LIMB
A22. Roman answer to bonus marchers. ~ NON
A23. Family saplings. ~ SCIONS
A25. Hipless fish. ~ EELS
A27. No friend of ours. ~ ENEMY
A29. He raised a swell crop of these last summer. ~ WEEDS
A32. Liquid asset (feminine) ~ TEAR
A35. Doggy rear ends. ~ TAILS
A37. Economic animal. ~ WOLF
A39. Unit of horsepower. ~ OAT
A40. Portugese sunshine. ~ REI
A41. This will preserve your bearings or scramble them. ~ OIL
A42. This is not a Hungary school. ~ ETON
A44. The only thing the world is together in. ~ ATLAS
A46. Esthetic? Teddibly. ~ ARTY
A47. Hands across the seat. ~ SPANK
A49. All China will ever get from the open door. ~ DRAFT
A51. You can make a bass fiddle with this. ~ BAIT
A53. Battered target of the Seraglio. ~ SULTAN
A56. The old June-bug frier at the cross-roads. ~ ARC
A59. A little ginger— ~ SNAP
A61. Fueling boat. ~ COALER
A63. 18 is the correct ring. ~ CARAT
A65. How Willie grew after his first cigar. ~ PALE
A67. A quiet bight. ~ COVE
A68. Fatal humor. ~ IRONY
A69. Anytime will do. ~ EVER
A70. A joint at the end of the bvd. ~ KNEE
A71. Spangled with poetic but malarial moisture. ~ DEWY
A72. Diamond color. ~ RED
A73. Middle Age rock-breaker. ~ SERF

D1. Tempo di plumma. ~ SLOW
D2. Dishes out the Oolong. ~ POURS
D3. A glancing nerve. ~ OPTIC
D4. Tarter. ~ TESTIER
D5. What Chicagoans take for a long journey. ~ RAP
D6. The kind of report that gets you by the ears. ~ ORAL
D7. To give the "Oh, yeah?" ~ BELIE
D8. The gin-rickshaw. ~ CAR
D9. You said it, Deacon. ~ AMEN
D10. Town situated many decrees west of Greenwich. ~ RENO
D11. The Young one never amounted to much. ~ PLAN
D13. A little flier with a hot tip. ~ HORNET
D14. Intergovernmental raspberry exchange. ~ CABLE
D19. A hunk of millenniums. ~ EON
D21. Cat calls. ~ MEWS
D24. Mean on the I. Q. ~ SMART
D26. What to do for the gaping habit. ~ SEW
D28. A profit of olden days. ~ YIELD
D30. Salesmen want to hold this open. ~ DOOR
D31. And even if as small an opening as this occurs ~ SLIT
D32. They will insert this. ~ TOE
D33. What a movie extra does to fill the empty spots. ~ EATS
D34. On, Stanley, on. ~ ATOP
D36. Manufacturers of colored yarns. ~ LIARS
D38. The buzzer that keeps Dr. Seuss flitting. ~ FLY
D43. You can't do this and leave it alone. ~ NAB
D44. A relative adjective. ~ AKIN
D45. Uncle Zeke had many a blow across this. ~ SAUCER
D46. Has at. ~ ATTACKS
D48. Describing an offal mess. ~ NASTY
D50. For little Florence only. ~ FLO
D52. Come to the point. ~ TAPER
D54. How not to leave the babies when you go out. ~ ALONE
D55. No time. ~ NEVER
D56. A salt, and battery stuff. ~ ACID
D57. What a well cooked steak is for the breadliners. ~ RARE
D58. A blackbird. ~ CROW
D60. Tarviate. ~ PAVE
D62. A water hazard. ~ REEF
D64. Just grab us one at random. ~ ANY
D66. He did this wrong and took it on the shin. ~ LED


